+      "chars": 947,
+      "file": "corpus/08-hareet-ai.md",
+      "golden": null,
+      "heading": "How a change is made",
+      "id": "08-hareet-ai#9.2",
+      "kind": "section",
+      "text": "- `[P]` A bug starts as a failing test. During a fix, a hook stops the agent from editing tests: fix the code, not the test. — https://github.com/hareet/h4reet-ai/blob/main/.claude/hooks/protected-paths.sh\n- `[P]` An incident gets a note, with the eval that would have caught it. When the kill switch trips, the gateway drafts that incident itself, from a template, with no model call. — https://github.com/hareet/h4reet-ai/blob/main/services/gateway/src/incidents/draft.ts\n- `[P]` Before Hareet merges, a clean-room gate runs every check on an export of the branch, with the network cut off, so nothing an agent left behind can run. — https://github.com/hareet/h4reet-ai/blob/main/tools/gates/gate\n- `[P]` The agents work in a sandbox, on their own container engine, behind hooks that refuse pushing, merging, applying infrastructure, editing budgets, or reading secrets. — https://github.com/hareet/h4reet-ai/blob/main/.claude/hooks/bash-gate.sh"
